2026-11-13 19:06:06,029 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ## INVESTIGATION NARRATIVE: NIST Data Leakage Case
2026-11-13 19:06:06,029 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
2026-11-13 19:06:06,030 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] Forensic analysis of three digital media (PC hard drive, USB stick, and CD-R) recovered from an employee with username "informant" reveals a sophisticated, multi-stage data exfiltration operation resulting in the unauthorized removal of approximately 103 MB of confidential business documents from company networked systems. The attack demonstrates clear operational planning, deliberate concealment techniques, coordinated evidence destruction, and indicators of external coordination with government officials and suspicious third-party recipients.
2026-11-13 19:06:06,031 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### INVESTIGATION OVERVIEW
2026-11-13 19:06:06,031 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Case:** nist-data-leakage
2026-11-13 19:06:06,031 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Systems Analyzed:**
2026-11-13 19:06:06,032 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - PC Hard Drive (pc.E01): Windows 7 Ultimate, compromised system
2026-11-13 19:06:06,033 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - USB Stick (rm2.E01): SanDisk Cruzer Fit with 51 deleted exfiltrated files
2026-11-13 19:06:06,033 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - CD-R Media (rm3.E01): Write-once optical media labeled "IAMAN CD" with 9 burn sessions
2026-11-13 19:06:06,034 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Evidence Sources:** 88 indexed sources from bulk extraction, registry parsing, file system analysis, optical media forensics, and Google Drive sync logs
2026-11-13 19:06:06,034 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Total Findings:** 27 (5 critical, 15 high, 1 medium, 6 informational)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,034 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### ATTACK CHAIN CHRONOLOGY
2026-11-13 19:06:06,035 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **STAGE 1: DATA COLLECTION (January - March 2015)**
2026-11-13 19:06:06,035 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] User "informant" deliberately accessed company network shares at 10.11.11.128 (secured_drive) containing sensitive business data. Shell bag artifacts show targeted navigation to:
2026-11-13 19:06:06,036 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - "Common Data" folder (accessed 2015-03-22 14:52:22 UTC)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,036 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - "Secret Project Data" folder (accessed 2015-03-24 13:47:58 UTC)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,037 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The targeted access pattern combined with systematic file organization indicates deliberate collection rather than accidental data handling. Documents were curated across five business-critical categories: Design (2 files), Pricing Decision (4 files), Progress (3 files), Proposal (2 files), and Technical Review (6 versioned files).
2026-11-13 19:06:06,037 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **STAGE 2: CD-R STAGING (2015-03-24 20:54:16 to 20:57:03)**
2026-11-13 19:06:06,038 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The organized documents were written to optical media (IAMAN CD) with evidence of 9 separate burn sessions. UDF filesystem analysis recovered 17 files in deleted sessions (-7 through -1) containing the identical organized data structure. File timestamps:
2026-11-13 19:06:06,039 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Session -7: 2015-03-24 20:54:16 UTC (Design files)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,039 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Session -6: 2015-03-24 20:55:00 UTC (Pricing Decision files)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,039 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Session -5: 2015-03-24 20:55:18 UTC (Progress files)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,040 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Session -4: 2015-03-24 20:55:22 UTC (Proposal files)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,040 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Session -3: 2015-03-24 20:55:43 UTC (Technical Review files)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,041 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] - Current Session (0): 2015-03-24 20:57:00 UTC (only benign image files visible at seizure)
2026-11-13 19:06:06,041 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The persistence of only innocent image files (Koala.jpg, Penguins.jpg, Tulips.jpg - standard Windows sample images) in the current session while sensitive documents were deleted from earlier sessions indicates deliberate cover-up: presenting the CD as innocent while staging data for external transfer.
2026-11-13 19:06:06,042 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **STAGE 3: USB STICK TRANSFER (2015-03-24 09:59:27 to 10:00:18)**
2026-11-13 19:06:06,042 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] All 17 exfiltrated files were copied from CD-R to SanDisk Cruzer Fit USB stick in rapid succession (51 total files including duplicates and associated media). Files were immediately deleted using standard FAT filesystem deletion, leaving recoverable orphaned entries in $OrphanFiles. The rapid copy-then-delete pattern is consistent with staged media being used for portable data transfer before evidence removal.
